---
title: "Do-It-Yourself Salmon Poke Bowls"
source: "https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/263252/do-it-yourself-salmon-poke-bowls/"
author: "A Day In the Kitchen"
site: "Allrecipes"
description: "Do-it-yourself salmon poke bowls are easy with this flexible recipe any time you want a custom salmon poke bowl at home. The topping options are endless."
---

> Servings: 4 · Time: PT25M

Gather @cooked rice{4%cups}, @soy sauce{4%tablespoons}, @rice vinegar{4%teaspoons}, @sesame oil{4%teaspoons}, @chile oil{0.25%teaspoon}, @sashimi-grade salmon, cut into small cubes{0.75%pound}, @avocado, sliced, or to taste{1}, @red bell pepper, sliced, or more to taste{1}, @shelled edamame, or more to taste{0.25%cup}, @sheets dried seaweed, cut into strips, or to taste{4}, @pickled ginger, or to taste{1%tablespoon}, @furikake (Japanese nori seasoning), or to taste{1%tablespoon}, @chopped green onion, or to taste{2%tablespoons}, @sesame seeds, or to taste{1%tablespoon}.

Divide rice among four bowls.
Combine soy sauce, rice wine vinegar, sesame oil, and chile oil in a bowl; add salmon and toss to coat. Divide among the four bowls.
Top bowls with avocado, bell pepper, edamame, seaweed, pickled ginger, and furikake seasoning. Garnish with chopped green onion; sprinkle with sesame seeds.
